### Why This Is Asked
This question assesses fundamental Android architecture skills: persistence with Room, data flow through the Repository and ViewModel pattern, and UI binding with RecyclerView. It also verifies understanding of rotation resilience and basic event handling.

### Key Concepts
- Room entities and DAOs for local persistence
- Repository pattern for data abstraction
- ViewModel with LiveData for reactive UI updates
- RecyclerView with Adapter for efficient list rendering
- Basic input handling and state retention across configuration changes

### Code Example
```kotlin
@Entity(tableName = "tasks")
data class TaskEntity(
    @PrimaryKey(autoGenerate = true)
    val id: Long = 0,
    val text: String,
    val done: Boolean = false
)

@Dao
interface TaskDao {
    @Query("SELECT * FROM tasks")
    fun getAllTasks(): LiveData<List<TaskEntity>>

    @Insert
    suspend fun insert(task: TaskEntity)
}

class TaskRepository(private val taskDao: TaskDao) {
    fun getAllTasks(): LiveData<List<TaskEntity>> = taskDao.getAllTasks()

    suspend fun insert(task: TaskEntity) = taskDao.insert(task)
}

class TaskViewModel(private val repository: TaskRepository) : ViewModel() {
    val allTasks: LiveData<List<TaskEntity>> = repository.getAllTasks()

    fun addTask(text: String) {
        if (text.isBlank()) return
        viewModelScope.launch {
            repository.insert(TaskEntity(text = text))
        }
    }
}
```

## RecyclerView Implementation

- Create item layout XML with TextViews for name and email
- Extend RecyclerView.Adapter with custom ViewHolder class
- Override three required methods: onCreateViewHolder, onBindViewHolder, getItemCount
- Use ViewHolder pattern to avoid repeated findViewById calls
- Set adapter and LayoutManager on RecyclerView in Activity/Fragment

## Key Components

- **ViewHolder**: Holds references to view components
- **Adapter**: Bridges data with RecyclerView
- **LayoutManager**: Positions items (LinearLayoutManager for lists)
- **Data Binding**: Optional but recommended for cleaner code

```kotlin
class UserAdapter(private val users: List<User>) : 
    RecyclerView.Adapter<UserAdapter.UserViewHolder>() {

    class UserViewHolder(view: View) : RecyclerView.ViewHolder(view) {
        val nameText: TextView = view.findViewById(R.id.name)
        val emailText: TextView = view.findViewById(R.id.email)
    }

    override fun onCreateViewHolder(parent: ViewGroup, viewType: Int): UserViewHolder {
        val view = LayoutInflater.from(parent.context)
            .inflate(R.layout.item_user, parent, false)
        return UserViewHolder(view)
    }

    override fun onBindViewHolder(holder: UserViewHolder, position: Int) {
        val user = users[position]
        holder.nameText.text = user.name
        holder.emailText.text = user.email
    }

    override fun getItemCount() = users.size
}
```

